# Except the canonical web UI (served by Wails, embedded by lanternd).
!frontend/dist/
# Except the Wails asset placeholder (the copied index.html stays ignored).
!cmd/lantern-gui/frontend/dist/
cmd/lantern-gui/frontend/dist/index.html
# Generated Wails bindings (`wails3 generate bindings -d ./frontend/dist/bindings`
# from cmd/lantern-gui); regenerated by `wails3 dev`, HTTP fallback covers the rest.
cmd/lantern-gui/frontend/dist/bindings/
# Never generate into the canonical UI dir; keep it a single static file.
frontend/dist/bindings/
# Except Wails project scaffolding (Taskfiles, packaging) for lantern-gui.
!cmd/lantern-gui/build/

# Temp
tmp/
*.tmp

*.peer
*.lantern-state
.lantern-*.part

# Audit artifacts from the code audit: a self-contained HTML report and the
# rendered charts. These are working output rather than documentation, and they
# are large and regenerable, so they stay out of the tree. Everything else under
# docs/ is documentation and is tracked — in particular docs/adr/, which README
# links to. Ignore the artifacts by name, not the directory.
docs/audit.html
docs/charts/